  "_construction": "Build scripts/pcn_ground_truth.json from evidence, not from a run's say-so.\n\nCONSTRUCTION, stated so it can be audited:\n\n  An MPN enters ground truth only if it is VERBATIM PRESENT in the source PDF's\n  text layer. That is an independent check \u2014 the string is on the page or it is\n  not \u2014 and it is what separates a real extraction from a misread. 893 of the\n  896 MPNs the 2026-09-23 run emitted pass it.\n\n  The three that do not are handled explicitly, never silently:\n\n  - SYTYD-122HP-1+ (PCN23-002) is a MISREAD of a crop clipped 47% through its\n    glyphs. It is excluded, and the part it misreads, SYTX9-122HP-1+, is added\n    by hand: it IS verbatim in the source, it is the documented eighteenth part,\n    and no run has yet emitted it.\n  - TYC's two composite cells hold two customer part numbers each in one string\n    (\"TYC1056344-1,\\n9501815SP-1\"). Their CONTENT is real \u2014 both halves are on\n    the page \u2014 but their SHAPE is wrong. They are included so TYC's total is the\n    documented 24, and flagged `malformed` so the scorer reports them separately\n    rather than scoring them as clean.\n\n  Every resulting per-notice count is then checked against the counts in\n  docs/pcn-corpus-validation-2026-09-21.md. A disagreement aborts.\n",
